  "limits": "Synthetic-control positive control only. It shows that guidance can reach a solver and make arms A and B distinguishable; it does not show that any guidance is better, is not native evidence and is excluded from every D4 verdict and method claim. The scenarios are owned abstractions of the anchor tests (step lists, checkpoint and drift flags), not executions of the anchors, and the A/B difference is produced by a frozen mapping written for this control. No arm C exists (R8 deferred) and no A/B/C comparison was made. Unmet section 5 acceptance: no HAR Unit, oracle verdict, denominator or cost was produced, so end-to-end propagation through T011/T012/T003 is not shown. The double reads a fixed GUIDANCE_PATH rather than a manifest's allowedComponentPaths, so a candidate with any other component is refused rather than partially read, and reads arm-A/B bytes from the roster draft that the freeze record binds by hash. No host, model, network, clock or paid route was used. Pre-PR reviews were run by Claude subagents and are not independent Luna review."
